60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Candidate D reminds me of the steady, descriptive work that has historically provided the most lasting value to the community.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Candidate A is the most viable. I saw that the glasshouse crew is at full strength, making the greenhouse trials feasible.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Victoria,,I must disagree. I found the glasshouse blocks are booked solid for two more cycles. Candidate A will be stuck in a queue for years.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Candidate C is the most economically sound. It leverages the free national computing agreement for its simulations, minimizing the awardee's financial risk.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Midori,,Candidate D is too risky. My research showed that field site records are plagued by environmental interruptions. A multi-climate atlas is a recipe for delays.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, I understand your fear, but the repository turnaround is now very fast. The data would be available to everyone quickly.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Victoria, if the glasshouse is full, then Candidate A is out. Candidate C requires spectroscopy, but does it require the broken instrumentation you mentioned?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"Yes, it does. Candidate C relies on the spectroscopy suite. With only one engineer for three institutes, the risk of downtime is unacceptable.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"A fair point. However, Candidate B's reliance on animal-unit day rates makes it a financial disaster. The costs will eat the grant in two years.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Midori,,"Candidate A is in a greenhouse, which is safer than the field, but if Victoria says the bookings are full, it's just another administrative bottleneck.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"Perhaps Candidate D is the most honest project. It is a catalog. It is steady, it is useful, and it doesn't rely on a single broken machine.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"I am looking for the path of least resistance. If the wet labs are understaffed and the machines are broken, we must look at the data-heavy options.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. Candidate D's primary requirement is the repository and the field sites. While the sites are volatile, they don't rely on a single failing engineer.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"While I prefer the efficiency of C, the operational risk Victoria highlighted is too great. Candidate D is the most viable, provided the budget covers the shipping.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Midori,,"I still worry about the field sites for Candidate D, but compared to the others, it seems the most resilient. It doesn't depend on a single point of failure.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I am glad we have found a path that ensures the research can actually be completed. I believe Candidate D is our best choice.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. It avoids the staffing crisis in the labs and the facility bottlenecks. It is the most reasonable choice.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I concur. It is the only proposal that doesn't land on a service that is currently at its breaking point.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,Logic dictates that the most viable project is the one that can actually be executed. I will cast my vote for Candidate D.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Midori,,"I agree. It's a balance of risks, and Candidate D's risks are the most manageable. I'll vote for D as well.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
